<title>ISRAEL: Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</title>
<headline>Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-06-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following shipments of grain have arrived or are due to arrive in Israeli ports, according to the inspection agency Hevra Klalit Lehashgaha (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	     ETA	   Cargo	    Quantity   Origin</p>
<p>Geroy Arsenala   unloading   maize grits     2,900     Europe</p>
<p>Liberty Spirit   unloading   soya	     43,691     U.S.</p>
<p>				     corn	     15,820</p>
<p>Bodaybo	    24/6	  feed wheat	2,700     Europe</p>
<p>Aspilos	    25/6	  sorghum	  22,770     U.S.</p>
<p>				     corn screening  6,018</p>
<p>				     corn gluten     2,855</p>
<p>Volgobal 148     28/6	  barley	    2,800     Europe</p>
<p>Ruja		  2/7	  feed wheat	1,600     Europe</p>
<p>Arnaki		7/7	  n/a		67,000     U.S.</p>
<p>Flag Nicolas	8/7	  corn	     23,524     U.S.</p>
<p>				     barley	    8,400</p>
<p>Matheus	    10/7	  wheat	    23,524     U.S.</p>
<p>				     gluten meal     6,900</p>
<p>				     gluten feed    13,700</p>
<p>Liberty Wave     20/7	  n/a		60,000     U.S.</p>
